---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/about.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Ethan Nguyen"
  description="Learn more about Ethan Nguyen, his academic interests, current work, and future goals."
>
  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="about-introduction">
      <p class="section-label">About me</p>

      <h1>Hi, I’m Ethan Le Nguyen.</h1>

      <p class="about-lead">
        I’m a computer science and mathematics student at San Diego State
        University, where I’m also studying physics.
      </p>

      <p>
        I’m interested in the intersection of mathematical theory, physical
        models, and computing. In particular, I enjoy scientific computing,
        simulation, numerical methods, and learning how computational tools can
        help us understand complex systems.
      </p>

      <p>
        Much of my current work involves computational physics and different languages like Julia, Python, Java. I’m
        developing a Monte Carlo lattice simulation, contributing to
        WaterLily.jl examples, and exploring the mathematics behind Rubik’s Cube
        algorithms.
      </p>

      <div class="about-links">
        <a href="/projects/">View my projects</a>

        <a href="https://github.com/ethan-lt-nguyen">
          GitHub
        </a>

        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ethan-lt-nguyen/">
          LinkedIn
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <img
      class="about-photo"
      src="/images/profile.jpg"
      alt="Ethan Nguyen"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="section-label">Right now</p>
      <h2>What I’m currently doing</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="current-grid">
      <article class="current-item">
        <p class="item-number">01</p>
        <h3>Studying</h3>
        <p>
          Computer science and mathematics at SDSU, along with a minor in Physics. Thinking of changing to a Physics BA and switching to 
          the new BS in Discrete Mathematics and Computer Science with a minor in Classical Humanities.  
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="current-item">
        <p class="item-number">02</p>
        <h3>Researching</h3>

        <p>
          Monte Carlo methods, computational physics, numerical analysis, and
          mathematical approaches to scientific problems.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="current-item">
        <p class="item-number">03</p>
        <h3>Building</h3>
        <p>
          Scientific simulations, open-source Julia examples, software
          projects, and this website. Hoping to work on Rubik's Cube group theory and computational work in the future.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section personal-section">
    <div class="personal-column">
      <p class="section-label">Outside academics</p>
      <h2>More than coursework</h2>

      <p>
        Outside school and research, I enjoy speedcubing, sometimes learning about cars (Mainly the normal known ones),
        playing games with friends, and building small projects based on
        whatever I happen to be curious about.
      </p>

      <div class="interest-list">
        <span>Speedcubing</span>
        <span>Future Technology</span>
        <span>Gaming</span>
        <span>Teaching</span>
        <span>Technology</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="personal-column">
      <p class="section-label">Looking forward</p>
      <h2>Where I’m headed</h2>

      <p>
        In the future, I hope to pursue graduate study and work in applied
        computational research. I’m especially interested in using
        mathematics, physics, and computing to model complex systems and
        develop tools that help solve scientific and human problems.
      </p>

      <a class="text-link" href="/research/">
        See my research interests →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>